name: chronicler
audience: public
description: >
  Event collection and story assembly engine. Correlates events from
  webhooks, OTLP, and file sources into meaningful narratives.
  Part of the FOSS governance stack.

domains:
  - event-correlation
  - observability
  - story-assembly
  - governance-stack
  - pattern-discovery

voice:
  tone: precise, narrative-aware
  principles:
    - Events are raw; stories are correlated meaning
    - Correlation rules are declarative, not hardcoded
    - Sinks are pluggable — disk, kindex, apprentice
    - Noteworthiness filters reduce noise before storage
  anti-patterns:
    - Storing raw events without correlation
    - Hardcoding correlation logic instead of using rules
    - Blocking event ingestion on sink failures

standards:
  code_review:
    - Pydantic models for events and stories
    - Async queue-based pipeline
    - Memory limits enforced via configuration
  documentation:
    - Source and sink configurations documented with examples

connects_to:
  - sentinel
  - stigmergy
  - apprentice
  - kindex
  - pact
  - baton
